set.body:
Objective: restore the fitted projection operations that were not carried through the legacy-map purge, and carry the completed variational language from representation and lowering into executable, fold-safe statistical programs.

Projection track:
- freeze distinct semantics for full projection, partial contribution, partial least-squares score recovery, supplementary-variable projection, reconstruction, and paired transfer;
- add identity-bound feature restriction, supplementary-variable frames, capability-gated synthesis, and a fitted multiblock projection facade;
- recover multivarious parity without recreating MvMap, Decoder, BiProjection, or CrossProjection as a parallel numeric layer.

Variational track:
- add a generic numerical solver boundary in linalg and a typed OperatorProgram compiler in multivar;
- integrate exact quadratic and equality programs first, then nonsmooth and constrained frames;
- provide a reusable ModelSpec FoldPipeline that fits, lowers, solves, certifies, and transforms entirely within each training fold.

Constitutional rules:
- Op, FunctionalFrame, OperatorProgram, and typed provenance remain the single semantic core;
- partial contribution and least-squares recovery are different public operations;
- reconstruction and transfer require explicit synthesis capability;
- parameterization, penalty, constraint, and operator shrinkage remain distinct;
- unsupported solver capabilities fail before iteration;
- shared code remains portable and every slice passes JVM and Scala.js tests.

Closure requires all finite children, parity and independent numerical oracles, IR and documentation alignment, and clean-worktree compileAll testAll.
